  "notes": "Cash-basis village; combined Statement of Activities / fund statement (p2) with General, Street (governmental) and Utilities (business-type) columns; governmental lines taken from the Total column where the Utilities column is blank, otherwise General + Street (computed). Governmental fund balance: 435,519 + 349,827 - 323,830 + 30,000 - 30,000 = 461,516. Business: 490,677 + 247,042 - 290,795 = 446,924. 'Taxes' 114,591 has no tax-type breakdown in the trimmed PDF, kept taxes. Ending cash from the p1 balance sheet (cash lines; CDs as investments); no beginning cash printed. Detail: General and Street from the budgetary comparison schedule (p3); the Utilities Fund from the more detailed Water/Sewer/Drop Off schedule (p5) instead of the Utilities budget column (no double counting). The 5-year comparative schedule (p4) repeats statement totals and is not recorded. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
